SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live at Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall (Saturday)
DTSTAMP:20260724T105419Z
DTSTART:20260725T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nAli Wong is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of her gene
	ration. Known for her fearless\, raw\, and unapologetically honest humor\,
	 she burst into mainstream consciousness with her Netflix specials Baby Co
	bra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while she was visibly 
	pregnant — a bold comedic choice that became her signature. \nHer comedy d
	ives deep into marriage\, motherhood\, sex\, and the immigrant experience 
	with a sharp wit and zero filter. She has since starred in the Netflix rom
	antic comedy film Always Be My Maybe (2019)\, which she co-wrote\, and the
	 critically acclaimed Hulu series Beef (2023)\, for which she won an Emmy 
	Award. Ali Wong is a true force in comedy — and her live shows are legenda
	ry for their energy and intimacy. \nThis Saturday show was added after the
	 Friday July 24 show sold out almost immediately — a testament to Ali Wong
	’s massive popularity in Hawaii and her deep connection to the islands. \n
	Event Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, July 25\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM HST (Doors
	 open earlier)\nVenue: Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall\, 777 Ward Avenue\, H
	onolulu\, HI 96814\nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes\nAge Restricti
	ons: All ages welcome\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hal
	l is Honolulu’s premier performing arts venue\, located at 777 Ward Avenue
	 in the heart of the city. Part of the iconic Blaisdell Center complex\, t
	he Concert Hall seats approximately 2\,158 guests and is renowned for its 
	excellent acoustics and intimate atmosphere despite its size. \nThe venue 
	features comfortable theater-style seating\, multiple concession areas\, a
	nd easy access to parking in the adjacent Blaisdell Center parking structu
	re. Valet parking is also available for added convenience. The surrounding
	 area offers a variety of dining and entertainment options\, making it eas
	y to turn the evening into a full night out in Honolulu. \nThe Blaisdell C
	oncert Hall has hosted some of the world’s biggest names in entertainment\
	, from classical orchestras to top-tier comedians. Its central location ma
	kes it easily accessible from Waikiki and downtown Honolulu. \nWhat to Exp
	ect\nAli Wong’s live show is a solo stand-up performance — no opening acts
	\, just Ali on stage delivering her signature brand of comedy for approxim
	ately 90 minutes. Expect a high-energy\, laugh-out-loud evening filled wit
	h stories about her life\, relationships\, and observations on modern cult
	ure. \nThis is the second and final Honolulu show — added specifically bec
	ause the Friday show sold out so fast. If you missed out on Friday tickets
	\, this is your chance. Arrive early to find your seats and enjoy the venu
	e’s amenities before the show begins. \nAli Wong’s Honolulu performances a
	re always special events. Her connection to Hawaii and her fans here makes
	 for an unforgettable night of comedy. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: 
	$100 – $127+ (resale prices may vary) \nPurchase official tickets directly
	 through Ticketmaster\, or find resale tickets through VividSeats for flex
	ible options including pairs and premium seating. \nOfficial TicketsResale
	 Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at
	 no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-a
	t-neal-s-blaisdell-concert-hall-saturday/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-neal-s-blaisdell-conc
	ert-hall-saturday/
LOCATION:Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall\, 777 Ward Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI\, 
	96814\, United States
